# Nest memory (mandatory)

Hooks enforce this workflow. Do not skip it.

## Before any implementation work

1. **`search_project_memory`** (`nest-memory`) — plans, crate boundaries, decisions.
2. **`search_context_memory`** or **`list_context_memory`** (`nest-context-memory`) with
   `session_key` = current git branch (or `branch:conversation`).

Until both run, **preToolUse blocks** edits, shell commands, and other non-memory tools.

## After every agent response

Call **`save_context_memory`** with:

- Summary of what changed this turn
- Files touched
- Decisions, blockers, open questions
- Verification commands and results

The **stop** hook issues a follow-up if you forget. Use the same `session_key` every time.

## Before compaction

Call **`save_context_memory`** with a full checkpoint. **preCompact** also auto-snapshots
the transcript, but an explicit agent save is still required.

## Optional

**`search_knowledge_base`** (`nest-knowledge`) when using Rust, egui, or eframe APIs.

**`search_knowledge_base`** with `collection="webos-tv"` when editing `apps/loon/client/`
(hook-enforced). See [webos-tv-knowledge.mdc](./webos-tv-knowledge.mdc).

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [tools/MCP-SETUP.md](../../tools/MCP-SETUP.md).
